// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: an ANONYMOUS `{ r: i32 }` object literal in a LAMBDA's inferred LIST
// return, in a module that declares BOTH a union ARM of that exact layout (`Circle`) and a
// standalone struct twin of it (`Dot`). `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics at all — not
// even a hint — and is the ONLY command that misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1,
// `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The FUNCTION and the message are
// the stable identifiers.)
//
// IT NEEDS BOTH TABLES TO CLAIM THE LAYOUT, and that is measured, each control ONE line
// different from this file:
//   · `Dot` DELETED                          → LOUD, `emitProgram: field access but no struct
//                                              type declared` — a clean reject, not this;
//   · `Sq` + `Shape` DELETED, so `Circle` is not an arm → RUNS, prints 7;
//   · the element ANNOTATED (`const o: Circle[] = [{ r: n }]`) → RUNS, prints 7.
// The third is the one that names the axis: the trigger is the ANONYMOUS spelling, not the
// list and not the lambda.
//
// IT IS THE SAME FAMILY AS D32 AND D33 AND A THIRD RUNG, and the direction is REVERSED, which
// is why neither fix reaches it. D32 was a declared ARM's element heap resolved through the
// STRUCT table; D33 was a declared ARM's name resolved onto a declared TWIN during
// monomorphizer substitution. Both are "a declared arm resolved onto a struct row". Here
// there is no declared arm in the expression at all — an INLINE literal is being resolved,
// and the two rows it could resolve to are a real struct and a real arm. D33's fix
// (`shapeNominalOfTy`'s arena VARIANT rung) cannot reach it for the reason its own census
// records: an anonymous shape has no DECLARATION identity, so `variantRowOfTy` correctly
// declines and the structural rungs below decide it. Probed at that site on this file's own
// program: `arenaS=-1 arenaV=-1 fsS=0 fsV=0` — both arena rungs decline, both structural
// rungs answer, and nothing in the arena can break the tie.
//
// THAT SAME PROBE READ ZERO ON THE WHOLE CORPUS AND ON D33'S 360-CELL GRID, and this file is
// one of the two constructed programs that proved the probe was live rather than dead. Both
// of those two RUN; this shape is the one where the tie is also a miscompile.
//
// It is `silent-class-inventory.md` D36, and it is NOT a regression: byte-identical on
// `235b365b` and on D33's branch, same function, same message.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty, which now names the
// closing change's own GRID as a fourth source.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }

function f() {
  const g = (n: i32) => {
    const o = [{ r: n }]
    return o
  }
  return g(7)[0].r
}

print(f())
